  "question": {
    "text": "A train moves towards a stationary observer with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>34</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The train blows whistle and its frequency is registered by the observer as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. If the train&#39;s speed is reduced to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> then the frequency registered is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If the speed of sound is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
